{"id": "EUVD-2026-108730", "enisaUuid": "3441d094-7499-3de5-a34e-cf9f1fc9376e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncipso: adjust cached option offsets when removing CIPSO\n\ncipso_v4_skbuff_delattr() removes the CIPSO bytes but does not adjust\ncached offsets for options that follow them.\n\nFor example, with a valid 10-byte CIPSO option followed by a seven-byte\nRR option, parsing records rr at offset 30.  Removing CIPSO moves RR to\noffset 20, while the cached offset remains 30.  Consumers such as\nip_forward_options() and __ip_options_echo() then access the wrong bytes;\nthe latter may interpret packet data as the option length and copy it into\nfixed-size option storage.\n\nMirror cipso_v4_delopt() and subtract cipso_len from the srr, rr, ts and\nrouter_alert offsets when they follow CIPSO.  cipso_len is the distance\nthe first memmove() shifts those options.  The later header move and\nnetwork-header reset relocate the bytes and their offset base together.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:23:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:23:05", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b965977126a90e01825814c859ba4788691eddd3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2200fe1d6148b78e1b8f00f4b2bd47760015077f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e49d611a9cfbaac927b8fa80ebd4f6b1f37ada0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6d25ffca055a77787c21a36b66c253f76239411b"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99064"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "112791ef-a2ff-3893-9774-2b5f4f2e2fa7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "89aa3619d141d6cfb6040a561aebb6d99d3e2285 <6e49d611a9cfbaac927b8fa80ebd4f6b1f37ada0"}, {"id": "4c992c2f-ce6e-3bb8-8b52-2ee64e27b342", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "89aa3619d141d6cfb6040a561aebb6d99d3e2285 <2200fe1d6148b78e1b8f00f4b2bd47760015077f"}, {"id": "5fd22dde-3935-397e-b6ee-4adb3753e20d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6ebff649-ae8f-31cc-93cd-ac6fb2b4aa8d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "89aa3619d141d6cfb6040a561aebb6d99d3e2285 <b965977126a90e01825814c859ba4788691eddd3"}, {"id": "8a67311b-af37-3f3d-9a9f-ee68e41d27fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "9ae37cb5-c0d2-3097-ae1a-2780716d0b96", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "c0607523-40fa-3a80-8a26-0cd528b80dc1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10"}, {"id": "c1fdb9b5-c654-3e09-8072-b90aa05533eb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "f21dabff-f894-303e-aa93-cef34f1c3498", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "f7a60105-e9a3-3d1f-b1f4-ea36c4ac80d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "89aa3619d141d6cfb6040a561aebb6d99d3e2285 <6d25ffca055a77787c21a36b66c253f76239411b"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fe3c0870-989b-3b5e-bddf-fa0a051127a7", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}